 \section{Redesigned Extensor Route Geometry}\label{app:route_geometry}
 
-This section documents the geometry of the redesigned extensor route of record (Section~\ref{sec:ongoing}) as saved by the optimization run of record (\texttt{Vas\_Pam\_20mm\_Result\_20260925.mat}, the run cited in Table~\ref{tab:app_ext_seed}). Figure~\ref{fig:app_route_geometry} reproduces the optimizer's tiled route-geometry view from that results file: eight pose panels sweep the 100-frame solution, drawing full flexion ($\theta_{k}=-120.0^{\circ}$), the solver frame immediately before each of the six contact-elimination events, and full extension ($+10.0^{\circ}$). The panel angles are the last poses at which the released row is still active; the release angles of Table~\ref{tab:app_ext_seed} are the first poses at which each row is off, one pose spacing of $1.31^{\circ}$ later. Beyond the release schedule, the results file also carries a top-level \texttt{removedText} field reading `\texttt{-p8}'. This field is a plotting leftover rather than a route statement: the plotting block of \texttt{Opt\_run\_Ext.m} (lines 730--736) computes \texttt{removedText} only as part of each interior pose-panel title, naming the point released in the next frame, and the value left in the results file is the one from the last interior panel, the p8 release-event panel at $+6.06^{\circ}$ in Figure~\ref{fig:app_route_geometry}. The route of record does contain p8: like p3, released at $+6.1^{\circ}$, p8 stays active from full flexion through 97 of the 100 design-grid frames until its release at $+7.4^{\circ}$ near full extension (Table~\ref{tab:app_ext_seed}), so the seed table and release schedule document the route as run. Each panel draws the active p1:p9 route in the femur frame (tibia-side rows transformed through the ICR) over the femur-cylinder, femur-wall, corrected-condyle, and tibia clearance envelopes of the route-elimination rule, with the local bend-radius checks at p2 and p8 drawn dashed. The optimized endpoint values of this design are $\mathbf{p}_{1} = [40.0,\,137.0,\,0]$~mm (femur frame; the square marker of Figure~\ref{fig:app_route_geometry}) and $\mathbf{p}_{\text{End}} = [34.4,\,-197.1,\,0]$~mm (tibia frame; the diamond marker), with resting length \qty{827.7}{\mm} and \qty{36.8}{\mm} of tendon.
